# ORDER-BLIND. t87_observer_named_fn pins only the define-first direction
# (env misses fall back to the opaque band while the name is a function;
# the env number wins after the assigns execute). In THIS direction the VM
# rebinds the name to the FUNCTION at the define's execution point, but
# compiled functions execute nothing at their statement position -- the
# env kept the stale number and the AOT printed 4 where the VM prints
# <fn f>, both rc 0. Silent-wrong, phantom stale value.
#
# Envelope shape: the VM RUNS this (rc 0, prints stab=0 then <fn f>).
# Adjacent shapes whose only post-define uses are CALLS matched by
# coincidence (calls emit direct C calls, not env reads) and are refused
# by the same conservative rule.

f is 3.0
f is 4.0
print of ("stab=" + (str of (stable of f)))
